{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure","id":645929,"title":"Cure!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-30T15:24:38-07:00","id":645929,"title":"Cure!?","content":"Just wondering if anyone else has ever had a player that made a Kindred who wanted to be cured and if so how did you go about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7529-silentstaccato","name":"SilentStaccato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7529_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T16:22:42-07:00","id":646015,"title":"","content":"Not in a game I was STing, but I did play in a game once where one of the other players was looking for a cure. He kept a journal where he would record everything he learned in his pursuit of a cure. He looked to the Lancea et Sanctum, but found that God's plan for him did not include redemption. He studied with the Ordo Dracul, but found that their goals of rising above their condition were incompatible with his desire to become human again. He sought out a Mage, but even the Awakened had no knowledge of a cure. But all the while, he kept writing in the journal. Eventually, the journal began to write back. It told him it could help him find what he was seeking. I don't know all the stuff he did on instruction of the thing he was communicating with, because this was like a 30-person LARP, but I do know a lot of it was pretty messed up. Anyway, it turned out he was unknowingly communicating with his own Beast, which was instructing him on how to separate them from each other. First he became a Hollow, and as he continued to follow its instructions, he steadily grew weaker as his Ka grew stronger. That game ended prematurely due to the ST running into some serious real-life issues, but the idea was that eventually he would have become human, and his Beast would have existed independently of him as something between a Ka and a Strix, which would have caused a lot of problems for the domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T17:15:03-07:00","id":646116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=646015#post646015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not in a game I was STing, but I did play in a game once where one of the other players was looking for a cure. He kept a journal where he would record everything he learned in his pursuit of a cure. He looked to the Lancea et Sanctum, but found that God's plan for him did not include redemption. He studied with the Ordo Dracul, but found that their goals of rising above their condition were incompatible with his desire to become human again. He sought out a Mage, but even the Awakened had no knowledge of a cure. But all the while, he kept writing in the journal. Eventually, the journal began to write back. It told him it could help him find what he was seeking. I don't know all the stuff he did on instruction of the thing he was communicating with, because this was like a 30-person LARP, but I do know a lot of it was pretty messed up. Anyway, it turned out he was unknowingly communicating with his own Beast, which was instructing him on how to separate them from each other. First he became a Hollow, and as he continued to follow its instructions, he steadily grew weaker as his Ka grew stronger. That game ended prematurely due to the ST running into some serious real-life issues, but the idea was that eventually he would have become human, and his Beast would have existed independently of him as something between a Ka and a Strix, which would have caused a lot of problems for the domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, now that's intense. haha; I mean I've seen a cure happen before. It was in a game i wasn't STing (and thank god for that) The ST in that game was just bad, he just had him get cured by a mage. That was it, just paid for it, no story no nothing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7529-silentstaccato","name":"SilentStaccato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7529_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T17:24:03-07:00","id":646128,"title":"","content":"I could see the desire to be cured being a good character trait, like an obsession, but as a ST I don't think I would ever complete and as a player it would be the end of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T22:20:20-07:00","id":646356,"title":"","content":"The vampire chronicles guide has a section about the quest for mortality, you might want to look at that, if you haven't already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T06:56:51-07:00","id":646617,"title":"","content":"Golconda is a pretty standard vampire plot. Generally (for Requiem) I send them off into the Ordo Dracul and have the Ladder keep an eye on them - they're basically the closest thing to an organized group of Golconda seekers we have in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T00:21:08-07:00","id":647750,"title":"","content":"But Golconda is not necessarily about becoming human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T04:28:21-07:00","id":647836,"title":"","content":"Not necesarily, but it is a common option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T04:49:26-07:00","id":647858,"title":"","content":"In 2e the Ordo consider becoming human a step backwards. They're supposed to get rid of the annoying bits of vampirism <i>without</i> losing the cool powers and immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:13:29-07:00","id":647953,"title":"","content":"I'm sure they'd consider a way to become human a development worth studying even if they wouldn't want to try it on themselves. Especially if they could do it to vampires who <i>hadn't</i> volunteered...<br /> <br /> <b>The Red Sign</b>, one of the last books for <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> Revised, presents an occult method of becoming human again, various groups seeking it, and various ways that a cured vampire might feature in an ongoing game. Obviously they're a substantial breach of the Masquerade in either setting, so in most cases the character would have to be written out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:30:42-07:00","id":647982,"title":"","content":"I don't think a cure should be possible. Vampirism isn't a disease or a virus, it's a mystical state of being. Vampires are undead, their bodily organs are atrophied and their blood no longer flows regularly. It's not like a scientist can whip up some miracle drug that turns them human again. Even if they could, the subject would probably die within seconds due to complete organ failure.<br /> <br /> Realizing that the embrace is permanent is kind of what makes being a vampire seem like so much of a curse and could explain why choosing to embrace somebody is a strain on their humanity. If becoming a human again were possible or easy, then life as a vampire wouldn't be as big a deal as its portrayed as. Then, of course, there's the fact that now that you're human again, you know too much and could endanger the masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-01-2015, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:36:30-07:00","id":648014,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;possible but not really worth it&quot; is acceptable. There are such immensely powerful entities in the world of darkness that <i>nothing</i> is truly impossible if you are willing to become indebted to beings that you really shouldn't want to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:45:24-07:00","id":648021,"title":"","content":"Gotta agree with Nyrufa. In Masquerade the emphasis was placed more on the curse aspect of it, where it was an actual curse, passed down by God. But in Requiem the whole point is, 'You're a vampire, now what?' And, 'not be a vampire,' sort of throws that out the window. Making the best of it should be the goal, whether it's overcoming the weaknesses of the condition or accepting yourself as gifted by the Crone or having a place in Gods graces, or just spiraling down until you're a draugr.<br /> <br /> So I was pleased Golconda wasn't mentioned in the second edition book, and am hoping it doesn't pop up again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:53:33-07:00","id":648033,"title":"","content":"We're missing an obvious answer here:<br /> <br /> Of course you can cure your vampirism. It just leaves you in the condition you were in just before it took effect. Y'know, a corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T08:12:03-07:00","id":648038,"title":"","content":"Draugyr is another cure depending on your point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T09:06:46-07:00","id":648071,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the Ordo Dracul already have a Coil in one of the upcoming supplements that, at five dots, turns you fully human again for a day?<br /> <br /> Isn't that same coil considered to be completely heretical and wrong and grounds for Bad Things to happen to you for using it?<br /> <br /> If you want to have a cure in your setting, I don't think mainstream Ordo should be where you find it.<br /> <br /> Though I'm with the others in thinking that a cure should probably not be possible, and I'm glad Golconda is gone. It shouldn't have ever left Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T10:49:50-07:00","id":648154,"title":"","content":"I think wether or not a cure is possible is pretty tangential to the &quot;search for a cure&quot; story. If a player wants to play a vampire who's looking for a cure, they probably don't want to find it very quickly, if at all, because being a vampire is still a central part of that concept. The cure should be found at the end of the chronicle, if it's found at all. But conversely to Nofather, I think &quot;<i>try</i> to not be a vampire&quot; is a perfectly valid answer to the question the setting poses of &quot;you're a vampire, now what?&quot; Seems like a pretty realistic reaction to me, never mind the fact that all the other vampires tell you it's impossible. Do you believe them and give up searching, or do you tell them they just think that because they haven't found a way yet? What lengths will you go to in your quest for mortality?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T10:51:33-07:00","id":648156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=648033#post648033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're missing an obvious answer here:<br /> <br /> Of course you can cure your vampirism. It just leaves you in the condition you were in just before it took effect. Y'know, a corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's right, you have to die before you become a vampire. Your vitae is the only thing that lets you get up and move anymore. You don't drink blood, you go comatose.<br /> <br /> Like I said, if you did become a human, you'd face total organ failure within seconds. It's one of those bitter sweet victory conditions. Yeah, you're not a monster anymore, but you're going to die soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T12:17:36-07:00","id":648241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SilentStaccato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure#post645929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering if anyone else has ever had a player that made a Kindred who wanted to be cured and if so how did you go about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the Ordo Dracul develop a &quot;daywalker treatment&quot; which temporarily lowered the subject's blood potency to 0 and revitalized their body. This would basically make them the equivalent of a Ghoul which could perform the Kiss. It was considered a failed project by the Ordo because the subject lost too much power, but they found a market for the treatment among young outsider kindred, who used the process to extend their masquerade into the day and to recapture a sense of normalcy after their embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T11:05:00-07:00","id":649125,"title":"","content":"In my view it should be possible, but it should always have a cost. The Beast separating into a Strix-thing mentioned earlier in the thread is a good one, and I might use it if a player goes for a similar route to becoming human, but other ideas I've had or seen are:<br /> <br /> -One of the key parts of the cure is 100 years of voluntary torpor. Unlike usual the dreams are relatively pleasant, and the vampire awakens on the first day of the 101st year of torpor, completely human. In a world that thinks they don't exist, and that they don't understand. Try opening a bank account, I dare you.<br /> -There is a cure for vampirism, but it turns you into something not human. The one I like is the idea of complete synthesis with the Beast turning you into another kind of creature.<br /> -You must sacrifice everybody you know and love to whatever ancient horror created kindred. You'll become a human. With Integrity 1, likely some serious mental scars, and a horde of vengeful ghosts. Have fun.<br /> -The only cure is to die and be reborn as a human, losing all memories of your current life, as everyone does.<br /> -The only way is to become some other sort of supernatural creature. I like the idea of it being a Strix or a Geist (the latter possibly being a sweet deal).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:41:31-07:00","id":649327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=649125#post649125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The only cure is to die and be reborn as a human, losing all memories of your current life, as everyone does.<br /> -The only way is to become some other sort of supernatural creature. I like the idea of it being a Strix or a Geist (the latter possibly being a sweet deal).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Unless we're going by the traditional belief that vampires have no souls, in which case they merely cease to exist when they die. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Oooh, here's an idea, surgically replace all your atrophied organs with healthy transplants and then jump start your heart.<br /> <br /> No wait, the blood transfusion would turn to vitae, and you'd regenerate during the day...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:03:01-07:00","id":649347,"title":"","content":"We <i>know</i> vampires have souls. They can <i>eat them.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T21:16:33-07:00","id":649734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=647982#post647982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a cure should be possible. Vampirism isn't a disease or a virus, it's a mystical state of being. Vampires are undead, their bodily organs are atrophied and their blood no longer flows regularly. It's not like a scientist can whip up some miracle drug that turns them human again. Even if they could, the subject would probably die within seconds due to complete organ failure.<br /> <br /> Realizing that the embrace is permanent is kind of what makes being a vampire seem like so much of a curse and could explain why choosing to embrace somebody is a strain on their humanity. If becoming a human again were possible or easy, then life as a vampire wouldn't be as big a deal as its portrayed as. Then, of course, there's the fact that now that you're human again, you know too much and could endanger the masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you are saying, but you seem to be putting a bit to much science into a game about magical undead beings. (lets not even mention Mages). If we look at the game as a whole the other denizens of the WoD have referred to the kindred as a disease. Other diseases of a magical nature have found cures in the game via magic, science or both; i see no reason Umpirism would not be able to be cured. That being said i by no means would allow it to be &quot;easy&quot; and the one seeking a cure would never fully recover or be normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7529-silentstaccato","name":"SilentStaccato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7529_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T23:11:20-07:00","id":649786,"title":"","content":"I still don't think wether or not a cure is possible really matters much. Playing a character that wants to find a cure is about the search, not about actually finding it. Think of it like a game of Promethean - same idea, different details. The story is about trying to find a way to become human, nevermind that you may not ever actually achieve that goal. The interesting part is in chasing after leads, most of which probably turn out to be false, but what are you going to do, give up? Or do you chase after the next whisper of a rumor of a hidden page torn from an ancient tome that you heard might contain a clue that could potentially lead to the location of the stone tablet that supposedly tells of where to find the first half of the forbidden ritual that might be able to turn a vampire into a living human again? <i>Maybe this time it will turn out to be real!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T03:48:49-07:00","id":649909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or do you chase after the next whisper of a rumor of a hidden page torn from an ancient tome that you heard might contain a clue that could potentially lead to the location of the stone tablet that supposedly tells of where to find the first half of the forbidden ritual that might be able to turn a vampire into a living human again? <i>Maybe this time it will turn out to be real!</i> </div> </div> </div>How convulted. That's how chronicles are made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T14:54:51-07:00","id":651813,"title":"","content":"I recall something from the mage side of the house that curing it wouldn't generally be possible due to the &quot;sponsor&quot; of the template preventing it. Luna, Father Wolf, Caine (in 1E), etc.<br /> <br /> If you want to pursue it, Charlaquin is right: it should be the final event in the entire campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T15:04:06-07:00","id":651814,"title":"","content":"Not Caine. Probably. &quot;Who the hell is the Vampires' sponsor anyway?&quot; is one of the big mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T18:54:08-07:00","id":678393,"title":"","content":"I played in a game where one of the PCs was a Dragon and was desperate to be human again. He was a Dragon for Coils of the Beast so he would never frenzy on people again. It took a while but he found a mage who said he could make him human again. After doing a number of tasks for him (which some where really twisted and I use to this day in my own games) the mage ripped the vamp's consciousness out of his body and stuffed it a teenager the mage had kidnapped just for the purpose. Turns out...the mage was one of the Mad. Opps. Picked up a slight case of schizophrenia as he had to contend with the fragments of the body's old psyche jumbled up in his own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T01:08:36-07:00","id":678624,"title":"","content":"To me as an ST of both Classic and New WOD, the desire for a cure is always a way to make the character feel special. The problem being that pretty much every pop culture version of a vampire wants to be human again in one shape or form.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They want to be differet then thier peers. They want to be better than their coterie. There is a lots of story to be told of a vampire who wants to become human again, but it is never a good story to tell in a group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","user":"DeimosMasque","date":". 09-26-2015, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T03:00:12-07:00","id":678688,"title":"","content":"While I'd normally agree, but the Ordo Dracul does have entire faction devoted to human-becoming again. And, doing a search for humanity has as much personal plot potential as an Invictus social climber - VtR apparently needs to have some level of characters going off and doing their own thing. I feel like a character doing the Golconda thing isn't that much different than a character wanting Transcendence in general. <br /> <br /> We can ask how appropriate the Dragon types fit into a Vampire game in the first place, but I don't think that becoming human is too outrageous of a demand compared to other Ordo goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T03:08:46-07:00","id":678691,"title":"","content":"Too many and it starts looking a bit like Promethean though. <br /> <br /> Actually that might make for a decent crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T03:39:05-07:00","id":678700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=678691#post678691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too many and it starts looking a bit like Promethean though.<br /> <br /> Actually that might make for a decent crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy solution is simply not to use Promethean's system then.<br /> <br /> Promethean's system is about a half formed person attempting to forge their own path into a world that hates them merely by existing and succeeds by eventually gathering enough life exp to become the person that they aim to be.<br /> <br /> Vampire's doesn't support such a system from the get-go. Vampire assumes that you've had a mortal (and provided you stick around long enough, Kindred) history and holding on to the past is the thing keeping you from running off into the deep end.<br /> <br /> If Promethean's system involves going forward (gaining Milestones and the like), I can see Vampire's system going backwards. Spending time looking up various past stories, documents of days long past, wrangling occult secrets from insane gurus. All in a effort to tie touchstones together.<br /> <br /> That being said, said person's lifespan is going to be short. Just because your human now doesn't mean that the Requiem is done with you. You lost all your &quot;powers&quot;, lost your status as a Kindred in the dance of the dead, and now you have the attention of Kindred elders who would just love to have you as a trophy to hang in a closet for all their friends to gawk at.<br /> <br /> You may be done with the vamp life but the vamp life ain't done with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T10:11:15-07:00","id":679154,"title":"","content":"Curious how would the ordo dracul feel about a cure if it was found? I think even those who thought the desire for one was folly, would have a scientific interest in the existence of such a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T13:10:25-07:00","id":679289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=679154#post679154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious how would the ordo dracul feel about a cure if it was found? I think even those who thought the desire for one was folly, would have a scientific interest in the existence of such a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is that they would record the event as best of their ability and attempt to suss out any information leading to new coils and the like, quickly followed by ripping open the now turned human to see how the inner workings are and other things. This is a case study, one of a kind. They aren't going to let it walk away from them even if it means breaking legs or simply cutting them off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T21:52:41-07:00","id":679674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=679154#post679154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious how would the ordo dracul feel about a cure if it was found? I think even those who thought the desire for one was folly, would have a scientific interest in the existence of such a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd be all over it. Even if members would not be inclined to use themselves the fact that it exists is a quantum leap forward in terms of occult knowledge. They'd do everything they could to repeat it if possible. That opens doors. If they can repeated without too much difficulty it could allow you to switch clans. Or as a punishment, force you into being human again and locking you in a cell for the rest of your biological life, slowly growing old. If easily replicated, it could allow elders to cheat the pull of torpor. Getting to the point where you have to go under for the long sleep? Not anymore! Gives us one night and you're back to BP1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T22:10:09-07:00","id":679682,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, and has been mentioned earlier, the Coil of Ziva handles becoming more human. It succeeds, though not permanently, at the highest level. It's considered basically heresy. I think the Ordo would despise it. They want to remove the weaknesses of their condition, not the strengths. Becoming human again is the opposite of their goals. It's a devolution. Their goal is evolution. It's anathema to the Ordo Dracul. But that's my interpretation of the information we have thus far in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T03:42:11-07:00","id":679818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=678691#post678691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too many and it starts looking a bit like Promethean though.<br /> <br /> Actually that might make for a decent crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div> Promethean, from the start, has been a glorified Golconda chronicle using a different supernatural as a base. There are several supernaturals out there that effectively have paths to becoming human, so, by your logic, they all become a bit like Promethean? Does that mean a highly social Mage game is like Vampire? Or a magic-focused CtL game is like Mage? Speaking of, the story and legend focus of CtL and BtP is worth noting. Overlap happens by necessity - otherwise, we would only have the Big Three as game lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=679154#post679154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious how would the ordo dracul feel about a cure if it was found? I think even those who thought the desire for one was folly, would have a scientific interest in the existence of such a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> It depends on the faction. The Sworn of the Ladder would be overjoyed. The Sworn of the Locus would be horrified. The Sworn of the Mysteries might ban it as athanama to the goals of the Ordo as a whole. The Sworn of the Dying Light would drool over studying it. The Sworn of the Axe would probably roll their eyes, think it dumb, and likely won't care unless it offers an opertunity to line their pockets through the Right of Dibs Dracula gave them.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Ordo Dracul isn't some monotheistic entity like the Lancea et Sanctum. Its a disparate group of vampires with different approaches to Transcendence, and can't agree even on what that Transcendence is. Just &quot;its something past vampirism.&quot; Not all of them are cultish, not all of them are scientists (actually, only one third are sciency, the rest are warriors and socialites).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=679682#post679682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly, and has been mentioned earlier, the Coil of Ziva handles becoming more human. It succeeds, though not permanently, at the highest level. It's considered basically heresy. I think the Ordo would despise it. They want to remove the weaknesses of their condition, not the strengths. Becoming human again is the opposite of their goals. It's a devolution. Their goal is evolution. It's anathema to the Ordo Dracul. But that's my interpretation of the information we have thus far in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Coil of Ziva is a mix of the Coil of the Ladder and Coil of the Locus mixed into one. So, yeah, its kind of like a two way street there.<br /> <br /> I'd like to point out that its not so much opposite of their goals - remember, the second Bride agreed to join Dracula's order for the very reason of achieving humanity again. There's a reason why its a heresy - you don't bother to declare something a heresy because it doesn't happen. You make something a heresy because, somewhere, people frowned at it but it still happens anyways. There are lots of Ordo Dracul vamps who seek humanity through the Coils. Officially, its banned. Unofficially? One rule that the Ordo really takes seriously is the right of each member to decide their own path to Transcendence. Banning becoming human is like making suicide illegal. If you're successful, what are they going to do to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T07:38:29-07:00","id":680003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=679818#post679818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're successful, what are they going to do to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Embrace you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T19:06:16-07:00","id":680587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=680003#post680003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embrace you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Lord</i>, that's dark.<br /> <br /> Still, it's not like they're going to burn all your notes and knock down your Haven, and keep you in an oublie-<br /> <br /> ...ok, yeah, that's probably <i>exactly </i>what they'll do, but hey, at least they'll probably <i>keep </i>you after that- you just obtained the Holy Grail for a non-zero percentage of a number of very powerful people as a bargaining chip, not to mention the raw data. I mean, heresy's heresy, but that's a pretty good haul for one day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T19:23:44-07:00","id":680594,"title":"","content":"Finding someone who managed to get rid of all the weaknesses <i>and</i> the powers of a vampire is halfway to their end goal anyways.<br /> <br /> They would certainly be worth studying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T02:56:21-07:00","id":680849,"title":"","content":"With the small caveat - anyone who becomes mortal isn't going to just be sitting around waiting to be caught. They'll likely have money saved up, a lack of Predator Aura to reveal them as a vampire. Even with blood magic backing them up, finding someone who's turned mortal isn't going to be easy for vampires unless they deliberately wait around to show off. Just another face in the crowd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T04:02:15-07:00","id":680872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/645929-cure?p=680003#post680003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embrace you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you can find a volunteer to drink the blood of a cured ex-vampire... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","user":"Craig Oxbrow","date":". 09-28-2015, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"h